Subject: [PATCH] Register and package RISC-V UEFI protocol tests

Add the SCT category for the five standalone protocol tests and package
their black-box driver alongside the existing RISC-V boot protocol driver.
Use the generic-test interface so checks for a missing protocol still run.

diff --git a/uefi-sct/SctPkg/CommonGenFramework.sh b/uefi-sct/SctPkg/CommonGenFramework.sh
--- a/uefi-sct/SctPkg/CommonGenFramework.sh
+++ b/uefi-sct/SctPkg/CommonGenFramework.sh
@@ -448,6 +448,10 @@ then
     if [ -e $ProcessorType/RiscVBootProtocolBBTest.efi ]; then
       cp $ProcessorType/RiscVBootProtocolBBTest.efi              $Framework/Test/ > NUL
     fi
+    if [ -e $ProcessorType/RiscvUefiProtocolBBTest.efi ]; then
+      cp $ProcessorType/RiscvUefiProtocolBBTest.efi              $Framework/Test/ > NUL
+    fi
+
 
     # *********************************************
     # BRS test cases
diff --git a/uefi-sct/SctPkg/Config/Data/Category.ini b/uefi-sct/SctPkg/Config/Data/Category.ini
--- a/uefi-sct/SctPkg/Config/Data/Category.ini
+++ b/uefi-sct/SctPkg/Config/Data/Category.ini
@@ -91,5 +91,12 @@ Description   =
 [Category Data]
 Revision      = 0x00010000
+CategoryGuid  = 3EEB9C98-9A8A-47B0-B933-823893D0C6FB
+InterfaceGuid = 71652D04-BF38-434A-BCB8-6547D7FD8384
+Name          = GenericTest\RiscvUefiProtocolTest
+Description   = RISC-V UEFI protocol presence, GUID, revision and environment tests.
+
+[Category Data]
